% ---------------------------------------------------------------- gibbs_sampler
%
%   Metropolis-within-Gibbs: updates one coordinate at a time, each via a scalar
%   random-walk Metropolis step evaluated against the SAME joint log-density with every
%   other coordinate held fixed -- mathematically equivalent to a Metropolis step
%   targeting the exact full conditional p(x_i | x_-i), since the joint-density ratio
%   with everything else held fixed IS the full-conditional-density ratio. This is the
%   standard fallback used whenever a full conditional isn't conjugate/directly
%   sampleable (what BUGS/JAGS call "Metropolis-within-Gibbs"), not exact Gibbs sampling
%   via closed-form conditional samplers -- those are necessarily model-specific (they
%   need to know each conditional's actual distributional family) and aren't something
%   a generic engine driven only by a joint log-density can provide. Updating one
%   coordinate at a time (rather than proposing the whole vector jointly, as
%   RandomWalkMetropolis does) can mix substantially better when parameters live on very
%   different scales or are only weakly correlated.
%
%   Wraps the C++ class `datamunge::bayes::GibbsSampler`.

%!  gibbs_sampler_new(-Object:gibbs_sampler) is det.
%!  gibbs_sampler_new(+Options:gibbs_options, -Object:gibbs_sampler) is det.
%
%   Stores the sampler settings.
%
%   Calls the C++ constructor `datamunge::bayes::GibbsSampler`.
%
%   Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: Options = C++ default.
%
%   @arg Options Sampler settings.
gibbs_sampler_new(Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(680, [], [], [], Object).
gibbs_sampler_new(Options, Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(680, [Options], [], [], Object).

%!  gibbs_sampler_sample(+GibbsSampler, +LogPosterior:arbitrary_function, +InitialParams:list(float), -Result:gibbs_result) is det.
%
%   Runs warmup sweeps (adapting each coordinate's step), then num_samples sweeps.
%
%   Calls the C++ method `datamunge::bayes::GibbsSampler::sample`.
%
%   @arg LogPosterior Log density up to a constant; only evaluate() is used.
%   @arg InitialParams Starting point.
%   @arg Result Draws, per-coordinate acceptance rates and step sizes.
gibbs_sampler_sample(GibbsSampler, LogPosterior, InitialParams, Result) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(678, [GibbsSampler, LogPosterior, InitialParams], Result).

%!  gibbs_sampler_options(+GibbsSampler, -Result:gibbs_options) is det.
%
%   The options this GibbsSampler was configured with.
%
%   Calls the C++ method `datamunge::bayes::GibbsSampler::options`.
%
%   @arg Result The stored options.
gibbs_sampler_options(GibbsSampler, Result) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(679, [GibbsSampler], Result).

