cuckoo_search_options_set_population_size(CuckooSearchOptions, Value) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(1680, [CuckooSearchOptions, Value], _).

%!  cuckoo_search_options_discovery_rate(+CuckooSearchOptions, -Value:float) is det.
%
%   pa: fraction of the worst nests discovered/abandoned each iteration. Yang & Deb's original paper headlines 0.25, but this implementation's "replace a randomly chosen comparison nest" Levy-flight rule (faithful to the paper) homogenizes the population fast enough at pa=0.25 that convergence quality becomes sharply seed-dependent on smooth objectives (verified: only 6/30 seeds converged well at pa=0.25, population_size=25 on a simple 3D sphere). 0.4 -- still within the commonly-used literature range -- injects enough fresh diversity each iteration to fix this at the default population size (verified: 30/30 seeds). (float).
cuckoo_search_options_discovery_rate(CuckooSearchOptions, Value) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(1681, [CuckooSearchOptions], Value).

%!  cuckoo_search_options_set_discovery_rate(+CuckooSearchOptions, +Value:float) is det.
