% ---------------------------------------------------------------- differential_evolution
%
%   DifferentialEvolution on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface.
%   Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy trial replacement. Supports the declared rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run. O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate.
%   The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
%   coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws.
%   Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable
%   objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone
%   is not a uniform convergence certificate.
%
%   Wraps the C++ class `datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   const dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution optimizer;
%   std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
%   ==
%
%   *References*
%
%     - R. Storn and K. Price (1997), Differential Evolution - A Simple and Efficient Heuristic for global Optimization over Continuous Spaces, https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1008202821328

%!  differential_evolution_new(-Object:differential_evolution) is det.
%!  differential_evolution_new(+Options:de_options, -Object:differential_evolution) is det.
%
%   Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
%
%   Calls the C++ constructor `datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   const dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution optimizer;
%   std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500
%   ==
%
%   Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: Options = C++ default.
%
%   @arg Options Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by DEOptions.
%   @see `optimize()`
differential_evolution_new(Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(1716, [], [], [], Object).
differential_evolution_new(Options, Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(1716, [Options], [], [], Object).

%!  differential_evolution_optimize(+DifferentialEvolution, +Function:arbitrary_function, +Coordinates0:list(float), +LowerBound:list(float), +UpperBound:list(float), -Coordinates:list(float), -Result:float) is det.
%
%   Run DifferentialEvolution from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
%   Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy trial replacement. Supports the declared rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run. O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate.
%
%   Calls the C++ method `datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::optimize`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
%   dm::optim::DEOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
%   std::vector<double> x{0,0};
%   const auto value=dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
%   std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
%   ==
%
%   @arg Function Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output shapes.
%   @arg Coordinates0 Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.; C++ writes it back: Coordinates is the value after the call
%   @arg LowerBound Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.
%   @arg UpperBound Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than lower limits.
%   @arg Result Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
%   @throws error(native_error(invalid_argument, Message), _) (C++ `std::invalid_argument`): DifferentialEvolution::optimize: crossover_strategy must be 'binomial' or 'exponential'.
%   @throws error(native_error(native, Message), _) (C++ `std::exception`): Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.
%   @see `trace_optimize()`, de_options_new/1
differential_evolution_optimize(DifferentialEvolution, Function, Coordinates0, LowerBound, UpperBound, Coordinates, Result) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(1714, [DifferentialEvolution, Function, '$rosetta_slot'(0, Coordinates0), LowerBound, UpperBound], Result, Writebacks),
    '$rosetta_out'(Writebacks, 0, Coordinates0, Coordinates).

%!  differential_evolution_options(+DifferentialEvolution, -Result:de_options) is det.
%
%   Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
%
%   Calls the C++ method `datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::options`.
%
%   @arg Result Const option reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
differential_evolution_options(DifferentialEvolution, Result) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(1715, [DifferentialEvolution], Result).

