% ---------------------------------------------------------------- nelder_mead
%
%   NelderMead on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface.
%   Local simplex reflection, expansion, contraction and shrink search. Starts with per-coordinate displacements initial_simplex_scale and stops when simplex diameter and value spread are small. Those conditions do not prove stationarity or a global minimum. O(p^2) simplex storage.
%   The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
%   coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws.
%   Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable
%   objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone
%   is not a uniform convergence certificate.
%
%   Wraps the C++ class `datamunge::optim::NelderMead`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   const dm::optim::NelderMead optimizer;
%   std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 2000
%   ==
%
%   *References*
%
%     - J. A. Nelder and R. Mead (1965), A Simplex Method for Function Minimization, https://doi.org/10.1093/comjnl/7.4.308

%!  nelder_mead_new(-Object:nelder_mead) is det.
%!  nelder_mead_new(+Options:nelder_mead_options, -Object:nelder_mead) is det.
%
%   Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
%
%   Calls the C++ constructor `datamunge::optim::NelderMead`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   const dm::optim::NelderMead optimizer;
%   std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 2000
%   ==
%
%   Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: Options = C++ default.
%
%   @arg Options Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by NelderMeadOptions.
%   @see `optimize()`
nelder_mead_new(Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(1959, [], [], [], Object).
nelder_mead_new(Options, Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(1959, [Options], [], [], Object).

%!  nelder_mead_optimize(+NelderMead, +Function:arbitrary_function, +Coordinates0:list(float), -Coordinates:list(float), -Result:float) is det.
%
%   Run NelderMead from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
%   Local simplex reflection, expansion, contraction and shrink search. Starts with per-coordinate displacements initial_simplex_scale and stops when simplex diameter and value spread are small. Those conditions do not prove stationarity or a global minimum. O(p^2) simplex storage.
%
%   Calls the C++ method `datamunge::optim::NelderMead::optimize`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
%   dm::optim::NelderMeadOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
%   std::vector<double> x{0,0};
%   const auto value=dm::optim::NelderMead(controls).optimize(f,x);
%   std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
%   ==
%
%   @arg Function Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output shapes.
%   @arg Coordinates0 Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.; C++ writes it back: Coordinates is the value after the call
%   @arg Result Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
%   @throws error(native_error(invalid_argument, Message), _) (C++ `std::invalid_argument`): NelderMead: initial_simplex_scale must be positive; NelderMead: reflection must be positive; NelderMead: expansion must be greater than 1; NelderMead: contraction must be in (0, 1); NelderMead: shrink must be in (0, 1); NelderMead: tolerance must be non-negative.
%   @throws error(native_error(native, Message), _) (C++ `std::exception`): Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.
%   @see `trace_optimize()`, nelder_mead_options_new/1
nelder_mead_optimize(NelderMead, Function, Coordinates0, Coordinates, Result) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(1957, [NelderMead, Function, '$rosetta_slot'(0, Coordinates0)], Result, Writebacks),
    '$rosetta_out'(Writebacks, 0, Coordinates0, Coordinates).

