% ---------------------------------------------------------------- trust_region_newton
%
%   TrustRegionNewton on the HessianFunction callback interface.
%   Cauchy-point variant: clips a steepest-descent ray using gHg and the current radius. Accepts any strict objective decrease and doubles the radius, otherwise halves it. It does not compute a model-agreement ratio, dogleg step or exact trust-region subproblem. Stops on gradient norm or tiny radius; O(p^2) Hessian work.
%   The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
%   coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws.
%   Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable
%   objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone
%   is not a uniform convergence certificate.
%
%   Wraps the C++ class `datamunge::optim::TrustRegionNewton`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   const dm::optim::TrustRegionNewton optimizer;
%   std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 200
%   ==
%
%   *References*
%
%     - J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), Numerical Optimization, second edition, https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5. The implemented variant and stopping rules are specified above.

%!  trust_region_newton_new(-Object:trust_region_newton) is det.
%!  trust_region_newton_new(+Options:trust_region_newton_options, -Object:trust_region_newton) is det.
%
%   Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.
%
%   Calls the C++ constructor `datamunge::optim::TrustRegionNewton`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   const dm::optim::TrustRegionNewton optimizer;
%   std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 200
%   ==
%
%   Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: Options = C++ default.
%
%   @arg Options Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by TrustRegionNewtonOptions.
%   @see `optimize()`
trust_region_newton_new(Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(2165, [], [], [], Object).
trust_region_newton_new(Options, Object) :-
    '$rosetta_construct'(2165, [Options], [], [], Object).

%!  trust_region_newton_optimize(+TrustRegionNewton, +Function:hessian_function, +Coordinates0:list(float), -Coordinates:list(float), -Result:float) is det.
%
%   Run TrustRegionNewton from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
%   Cauchy-point variant: clips a steepest-descent ray using gHg and the current radius. Accepts any strict objective decrease and doubles the radius, otherwise halves it. It does not compute a model-agreement ratio, dogleg step or exact trust-region subproblem. Stops on gradient norm or tiny radius; O(p^2) Hessian work.
%
%   Calls the C++ method `datamunge::optim::TrustRegionNewton::optimize`.
%
%   *Example*
%
%   ==
%   dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
%   dm::optim::TrustRegionNewtonOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
%   std::vector<double> x{0,0};
%   const auto value=dm::optim::TrustRegionNewton(controls).optimize(f,x);
%   std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
%   ==
%
%   @arg Function Borrowed HessianFunction with matching finite output shapes.
%   @arg Coordinates0 Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.; C++ writes it back: Coordinates is the value after the call
%   @arg Result Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.
%   @throws error(native_error(invalid_argument, Message), _) (C++ `std::invalid_argument`): TrustRegionNewton: initial_radius must be positive.
%   @throws error(native_error(native, Message), _) (C++ `std::exception`): Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.
%   @see `trace_optimize()`, trust_region_newton_options_new/1
trust_region_newton_optimize(TrustRegionNewton, Function, Coordinates0, Coordinates, Result) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(2163, [TrustRegionNewton, Function, '$rosetta_slot'(0, Coordinates0)], Result, Writebacks),
    '$rosetta_out'(Writebacks, 0, Coordinates0, Coordinates).

%!  trust_region_newton_options(+TrustRegionNewton, -Result:trust_region_newton_options) is det.
%
%   Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
%
%   Calls the C++ method `datamunge::optim::TrustRegionNewton::options`.
%
%   @arg Result Const option reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.
trust_region_newton_options(TrustRegionNewton, Result) :-
    '$rosetta_call'(2164, [TrustRegionNewton], Result).

